==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|flum|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|flum|lang=fro}}, {{term|flun}}, from Latin {{term|flumen|lang=la}}, from {{term|fluere|fluere|to flow}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/fluːm/}}
* {{audio|en-us-flume.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[ravine]] or [[gorge]], usually one with [[water]] running through.
# An open [[channel]] or [[trough]] used to direct or divert [[liquid]]s.

